+++ b/docs-site/src/content/docs/guides/claude-code.md
@@ -307,0 +308,7 @@
+The picker relay accepts up to 128 unfinished uploads within its 256 in-flight request slots.
+An upload is cancelled after 30 seconds without body progress or five minutes without completion.
+An excess upload receives an empty 503 response; retry after capacity becomes available. These
+limits apply to HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2 request bodies only: completed uploads and long-lived response
+streams are not timed out by this rule. An expired HTTP/2 upload does not close sibling streams.
+There is no new setting or setup step.
+
