diff --git a/structure/clients/claude-desktop.md b/structure/clients/claude-desktop.md
index 6f4d595720035635fbb490c77d3cc20e40f62e75..d34eb129f833928cc04086b0a72b33caf61d33e0 100644
--- a/structure/clients/claude-desktop.md
+++ b/structure/clients/claude-desktop.md
@@ -215,0 +216,10 @@
+The shared relay admits at most 256 upstream requests, including at most 128 unfinished
+uploads across both HTTP versions. An upload has a 30-second no-progress deadline and an
+absolute five-minute completion deadline; receiving nonempty data refreshes only the former.
+HTTP/2 upload classification uses the initial HEADERS END_STREAM flag, not its method or
+Content-Length. Expiry cancels that stream (or the HTTP/1.1 request connection), destroys the
+upstream request and releases both slots once. Body completion clears both timers and the
+upload slot; long response/SSE streams retain only their ordinary upstream slot. Refused and
+early-closed uploads are destroyed rather than left as uncounted receivers. This preserves
+bodyless capacity against unfinished uploads, not against arbitrary sustained request floods.
+`tests/claude-integration/claude-picker-listener.test.ts` covers these limits and CONNECT routing.
